# API
PORT=5001
JWT_SECRET=change-me-in-production
# On the live server also set NODE_ENV=production — the app then REQUIRES a unique
# JWT_SECRET (32+ chars) and refuses to boot with the dev default.
# Generate one: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"

# Browser origin of the shop (CORS). Comma-separate if both subdomain and live domain are in use.
# This week: https://shop.bigdrop.co.ke
# Next week: https://bigdrop.co.ke
CLIENT_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173

# Set TRUE on the live server: the app sits behind cPanel's reverse proxy, so the real
# client IP arrives in X-Forwarded-For and rate limiting needs it. Leave unset locally.
# TRUST_PROXY=true

# Public shop URL used in password-reset emails and also added to CORS.
# PUBLIC_CLIENT_URL=https://shop.bigdrop.co.ke

# Keep live pictures outside the zip (do not put images in MySQL)
# UPLOADS_DIR=/home/USER/bigdrop-uploads

# cPanel MySQL (Database Wizard). Shop JSON is stored in table bigdrop_store.
# MYSQL_HOST=localhost
# MYSQL_PORT=3306
# MYSQL_USER=
# MYSQL_PASSWORD=
# MYSQL_DATABASE=bigdrop_store

# Optional JSON backup folder if MySQL is not set yet
# DATA_DIR=/home/USER/bigdrop-data

# Email (welcome, newsletter, password reset). Without these, mail is logged only.
# SMTP_HOST=mail.bigdrop.co.ke
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_SECURE=false
# SMTP_USER=orders@bigdrop.co.ke
# SMTP_PASS=
# SMTP_FROM=orders@bigdrop.co.ke

# M-Pesa Daraja (paybill). Without these, checkout uses a demo STK.
# MPESA_ENV=production
# MPESA_CONSUMER_KEY=
# MPESA_CONSUMER_SECRET=
# MPESA_SHORTCODE=
# MPESA_PASSKEY=
# MPESA_CALLBACK_URL=https://shop.bigdrop.co.ke/api/payments/mpesa/callback
# PUBLIC_API_URL=https://shop.bigdrop.co.ke

# Card payments (Paystack). Without this, card checkout is a demo.
# PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=
# PAYSTACK_CALLBACK_URL=https://shop.bigdrop.co.ke/checkout

# Africa's Talking SMS (purchase confirmations). Without these, SMS is logged only.
# AT_API_KEY=
# AT_USERNAME=
# AT_SENDER=

# Client (copy into client/.env). Point at the API the browser should call.
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:5001/api

# ── Oracom go-live (you click these in cPanel) ─────────────────────────────
# 1. This week: subdomain shop.bigdrop.co.ke → this Node app. Leave WordPress on bigdrop.co.ke.
# 2. Create MySQL via Database Wizard. Set MYSQL_* above. Do NOT run `npm run seed` on live data.
# 3. Set UPLOADS_DIR to a folder outside the zip so photos survive redeploys.
# 4. SMTP for orders@ / info@, then M-Pesa, Paystack, Africa's Talking.
# 5. Admin → Woo import: upload the WooCommerce products CSV while WordPress is still up
#    so photos download into UPLOADS_DIR (do not leave wp-content URLs in the shop).
# 6. Next week: point bigdrop.co.ke at this app. Update CLIENT_ORIGIN, PUBLIC_CLIENT_URL,
#    VITE_API_URL, M-Pesa callback, Paystack callback to https://bigdrop.co.ke …
# 7. Delete WordPress last (wp-content/uploads dies with it).
# Admin login on live: info@bigdrop.co.ke (password123 until you change it).
# Careers apply: info@bigdrop.co.ke · Customer orders: orders@bigdrop.co.ke
